summary:
  With this computer and a device playing together, the "Play on" menu's
  Mute switches the room's mute and the device plays on.

history:
  The mute on the room's knob is pactl's own switch, and its answer comes
  back on the same round trip. A click made beside a playing device marks
  that answer as one the devices follow: silent when it says muted, back at
  the master times their balance when it says not. Without the mark the
  mute is for half of what plays.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
          if (road === "sink") { to.sinkMute = true; to.castFollows = both; }

replace:
          if (road === "sink") { to.sinkMute = true; to.castFollows = false; }

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_the_mute_beside_a_device_is_for_both
  and tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_together_the_mute_silences_both_and_the_unmute_brings_both_back.
  Line-neutral.
